longseq-kuairand-bench

The HSTU implementation in longseq_bench/models.py adapts HSTU equations,
initialization and relative time/position bias from:

  Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates: generative-recommenders (Apache-2.0)
  USTC-StarTeam: FuXi-Linear, commit 5a704061a7ebf0b81afb465f12f93f2747ba4667
  https://github.com/USTC-StarTeam/fuxi-linear

The implementation has been changed to portable dense/tiled PyTorch operations,
with a common trainer and full-catalog scorer. It does not include the original
production kernels. Original copyright and Apache-2.0 notices are retained.

The DARE scorer is an independent implementation of the published method with
documented next-item-task adaptations. The original DARE repository is not
redistributed in the public package. The locally fetched author source under
vendor/ is excluded from the public export.

ULTRA-HSTU is an architectural adaptation from the published paper, not a release
of Meta's production implementation. SLA windows and the 3+1 truncation topology
are chosen benchmark hyperparameters, not claimed original production settings.

CCFormer (longseq_bench/ccformer.py) is independently implemented from the
published mechanisms in arXiv:2607.28070v1, not copied from an author repository.
It is a causal ID-only next-item adaptation: triangular temporal/subspace
projections, left-padded compression, history-derived user fields, a scalar head
and the common FuXi training/evaluation replace the original CTR setting.
No author-code, industrial-performance or paper-result reproduction is claimed.

Reference papers:
  HSTU: https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.17152
  DARE: https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.02604
  FuXi-Linear: https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.23671
  ULTRA-HSTU: https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.16986
  CCFormer: https://arxiv.org/html/2607.28070v1
